    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong>Table&nbsp;8.01 </strong>Terminology applied to anal and perianal dysplastic lesions</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Teri A. Longacre",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 496.2pt; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"662\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 165.4pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"221\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Description of lesion</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 165.4pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"221\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210050501;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">LAST</span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 165.4pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"221\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210050501;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">AIN</span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 165.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"221\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210050501;\"><strong>Condyloma acuminatum</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 165.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"221\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210050501;\">LSIL (condyloma acuminatum)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 165.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"221\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210050501;\">Condyloma acuminatum</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 165.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"221\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210050501;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Mild dysplasia (i.e. cytological atypia restricted to the lower one&nbsp;third of the epithelium and/or koilocytosis)</span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 165.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"221\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210050501;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">LSIL</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 165.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"221\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210050501;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">AIN-I</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 165.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"221\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210050501;\"><strong>Moderate dysplasia (i.e. cytological atypia restricted to two&nbsp;thirds of the epithelium)</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 165.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"221\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210050501;\">HSIL</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 165.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"221\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210050501;\">AIN-II</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 165.4pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"221\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210050501;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Severe dysplasia&nbsp;/ carcinoma in&nbsp;situ (i.e. cytological atypia more than two&nbsp;thirds of the epithelium)</span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 165.4pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"221\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210050501;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">HSIL</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 165.4pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"221\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210050501;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">AIN-III</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">AIN, anal intraepithelial neoplasia; HSIL, high-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion; LAST, Lower Anogenital Squamous Terminology; LSIL, low-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Note: Anal HSIL can be reported as HSIL (AIN-II) or HSIL (AIN-III), depending on the degree of dysplasia.</p>",
