    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "High-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "High-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion (anal squamous intraepithelial neoplasia III [AIN III]) shows full-thickness mucosal involvement by hyperchromatic cells with a high N:C ratio. Mitotic figures, including atypical forms, are seen in the upper two thirds of the mucosa.",
